-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: Subchapter V (stock and dividends), sections 167 and 168
-- (lost, stolen or destroyed certificates; proceedings in the Court of Chancery to compel a new certificate or uncertificated shares).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Sections 167 and 168 are among those that section 114(b)(2) takes out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a).
-- The Court of Chancery gets no seat: its orders are encoded as what they mean for the owner of the certificate (what the owner may apply for, what must be served, what the owner must give).
-- A judgment the section hands to the court ("if the court is satisfied") is an input.

§ `Section 167: lost, stolen or destroyed stock certificates; issuance of new certificate or uncertificated shares`

-- A corporation may issue a new certificate of stock or uncertificated shares in place of any certificate it issued that is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed.
-- src:574 | A corporation may issue a new certificate of stock or uncertificated shares in place of any certificate theretofore issued by it, alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed, and the corporation may require the owner of the lost, stolen or destroyed certificate, or such owner’s legal representative to give the corporation a bond sufficient to indemnify it against any claim that may be made against it on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction of any such certificate or the issuance of such new certificate or uncertificated shares.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 167 (src:574)
GIVEN `the certificate was issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 167 the corporation may issue a new certificate or uncertificated shares in place of the certificate` `the certificate was issued by the corporation` `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` MEANS
        `the certificate was issued by the corporation`
    AND `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed`

-- The corporation may require the owner of the lost, stolen or destroyed certificate, or the owner's legal representative, to give it a bond sufficient to indemnify it against any claim that may be made
-- on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction or the issuance of the new certificate or uncertificated shares.
-- src:574 | and the corporation may require the owner of the lost, stolen or destroyed certificate, or such owner’s legal representative to give the corporation a bond sufficient to indemnify it against any claim that may be made against it on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction of any such certificate or the issuance of such new certificate or uncertificated shares.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 167 (src:574)
GIVEN `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 167 the corporation may require the person to give a bond sufficient to indemnify it` `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` `the person is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative` MEANS
        `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed`
    AND `the person is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative`

§ `Section 168: judicial proceedings to compel issuance of new certificate or uncertificated shares`

-- Section 168(a): if a corporation refuses to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate in place of a certificate issued by it, or by a corporation of which it is the lawful successor,
-- alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed, the owner or the owner's legal representatives may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order requiring the corporation to show cause why it should not issue them.
-- src:578 | If a corporation refuses to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate of stock in place of a certificate theretofore issued by it, or by any corporation of which it is the lawful successor, alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed, the owner of the lost, stolen or destroyed certificate or such owner’s legal representatives may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order requiring the corporation to show cause why it should not issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate of stock in place of the certificate so lost, stolen or destroyed. Such application shall be by a complaint which shall state the name of the corporation, the number and date of the certificate, if known or ascertainable by the plaintiff, the number of shares of stock represented thereby and to whom issued, and a statement of the circumstances attending such loss, theft or destruction. Thereupon the court shall make an order requiring the corporation to show cause at a time and place therein designated, why it should not issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate of stock in place of the one described in the complaint. A copy of the complaint and order shall be served upon the corporation at least 5 days before the time designated in the order.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(a) (src:578)
GIVEN `the corporation refuses to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate was issued by the corporation or by a corporation of which it is the lawful successor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(a) the owner may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to show cause` `the corporation refuses to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate` `the certificate was issued by the corporation or by a corporation of which it is the lawful successor` `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed` `the applicant is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative` MEANS
        `the corporation refuses to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate`
    AND `the certificate was issued by the corporation or by a corporation of which it is the lawful successor`
    AND `the certificate is alleged to have been lost, stolen or destroyed`
    AND `the applicant is the owner of the certificate or the owner's legal representative`

-- The application is by a complaint stating the name of the corporation, the number and date of the certificate, if known or ascertainable by the plaintiff, the number of shares of stock represented and to whom issued,
-- and a statement of the circumstances attending the loss, theft or destruction.
-- src:578 | Such application shall be by a complaint which shall state the name of the corporation, the number and date of the certificate, if known or ascertainable by the plaintiff, the number of shares of stock represented thereby and to whom issued, and a statement of the circumstances attending such loss, theft or destruction. Thereupon the court shall make an order requiring the corporation to show cause at a time and place therein designated, why it should not issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate of stock in place of the one described in the complaint. A copy of the complaint and order shall be served upon the corporation at least 5 days before the time designated in the order.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(a) (src:578)
GIVEN `the complaint states the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number and date of the certificate are known or ascertainable by the plaintiff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint states the number and date of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint states the number of shares of stock represented by the certificate and to whom issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint states the circumstances attending the loss, theft or destruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(a) the complaint states what the subsection requires` `the complaint states the name of the corporation` `the number and date of the certificate are known or ascertainable by the plaintiff` `the complaint states the number and date of the certificate` `the complaint states the number of shares of stock represented by the certificate and to whom issued` `the complaint states the circumstances attending the loss, theft or destruction` MEANS
        `the complaint states the name of the corporation`
    AND (    (NOT `the number and date of the certificate are known or ascertainable by the plaintiff`)
         OR  `the complaint states the number and date of the certificate`)
    AND `the complaint states the number of shares of stock represented by the certificate and to whom issued`
    AND `the complaint states the circumstances attending the loss, theft or destruction`

-- Thereupon the court shall make an order requiring the corporation to show cause, at a time and place designated, why it should not issue the new uncertificated shares or certificate.
-- A copy of the complaint and order shall be served on the corporation at least 5 days before the time designated in the order.
-- src:578 | Thereupon the court shall make an order requiring the corporation to show cause at a time and place therein designated, why it should not issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate of stock in place of the one described in the complaint. A copy of the complaint and order shall be served upon the corporation at least 5 days before the time designated in the order.
-- src:578 | A copy of the complaint and order shall be served upon the corporation at least 5 days before the time designated in the order.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(a) (src:578)
GIVEN `the application is by a complaint that states what the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(a) the court shall make an order requiring the corporation to show cause` `the application is by a complaint that states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the application is by a complaint that states what the subsection requires`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(a) (src:578)
GIVEN `the day the copy of the complaint and order was served on the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the day designated in the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(a) the service on the corporation is timely` `the day the copy of the complaint and order was served on the corporation` `the day designated in the order` MEANS
    `the day the copy of the complaint and order was served on the corporation` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 5) `before` `the day designated in the order`)

-- Section 168(b): if upon hearing the court is satisfied that the plaintiff is the lawful owner of the shares described in the complaint (or any part), that the certificate has been lost, stolen or destroyed,
-- and that no sufficient cause has been shown why new uncertificated shares or a new certificate should not be issued, it shall order the corporation to issue and deliver them to the plaintiff.
-- The court's satisfaction is the court's judgment: an input.
-- src:579 | If, upon hearing, the court is satisfied that the plaintiff is the lawful owner of the number of shares of capital stock, or any part thereof, described in the complaint, and that the certificate therefor has been lost, stolen or destroyed, and no sufficient cause has been shown why new uncertificated shares or a new certificate should not be issued in place thereof, it shall make an order requiring the corporation to issue and deliver to the plaintiff new uncertificated shares or a new certificate for such shares. In its order the court shall direct that, prior to the issuance and delivery to the plaintiff of such new uncertificated shares or a new certificate, the plaintiff give the corporation a bond in such form and with such security as to the court appears sufficient to indemnify the corporation against any claim that may be made against it on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction of any such certificate or the issuance of such new uncertificated shares or new certificate. No corporation which has issued uncertificated shares or a certificate pursuant to an order of the court entered hereunder shall be liable in an amount in excess of the amount specified in such bond.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(b) (src:579)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the plaintiff is the lawful owner of the shares described in the complaint or any part of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the certificate has been lost, stolen or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no sufficient cause has been shown why new uncertificated shares or a new certificate should not be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(b) the court shall order the corporation to issue and deliver new uncertificated shares or a new certificate to the plaintiff` `the court is satisfied that the plaintiff is the lawful owner of the shares described in the complaint or any part of them` `the court is satisfied that the certificate has been lost, stolen or destroyed` `no sufficient cause has been shown why new uncertificated shares or a new certificate should not be issued` MEANS
        `the court is satisfied that the plaintiff is the lawful owner of the shares described in the complaint or any part of them`
    AND `the court is satisfied that the certificate has been lost, stolen or destroyed`
    AND `no sufficient cause has been shown why new uncertificated shares or a new certificate should not be issued`

-- In its order the court shall direct that, before the new uncertificated shares or certificate are issued and delivered, the plaintiff give the corporation a bond in such form and with such security
-- as to the court appears sufficient to indemnify the corporation against any claim made on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction or the issuance.
-- src:579 | In its order the court shall direct that, prior to the issuance and delivery to the plaintiff of such new uncertificated shares or a new certificate, the plaintiff give the corporation a bond in such form and with such security as to the court appears sufficient to indemnify the corporation against any claim that may be made against it on account of the alleged loss, theft or destruction of any such certificate or the issuance of such new uncertificated shares or new certificate. No corporation which has issued uncertificated shares or a certificate pursuant to an order of the court entered hereunder shall be liable in an amount in excess of the amount specified in such bond.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(b) (src:579)
GIVEN `the court has ordered the corporation to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 168(b) the plaintiff must give the corporation a bond before the new uncertificated shares or certificate are issued and delivered` `the court has ordered the corporation to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate` MEANS
    `the court has ordered the corporation to issue new uncertificated shares or a new certificate`

-- No corporation which has issued uncertificated shares or a certificate under an order of the court shall be liable in an amount in excess of the amount specified in the bond.
-- The most the corporation can be made to pay on a claim: the claim or the bond, whichever is less. If the shares were not issued under such an order the cap does not apply, which is NOTHING.
-- src:579 | No corporation which has issued uncertificated shares or a certificate pursuant to an order of the court entered hereunder shall be liable in an amount in excess of the amount specified in such bond.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 168(b) (src:579)
GIVEN `the shares or certificate were issued pursuant to an order of the court under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the claim made against the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount specified in the bond` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 168(b) the most the corporation is liable for on the claim` `the shares or certificate were issued pursuant to an order of the court under this section` `the amount of the claim made against the corporation` `the amount specified in the bond` MEANS
    IF `the shares or certificate were issued pursuant to an order of the court under this section`
    THEN JUST (min `the amount of the claim made against the corporation` `the amount specified in the bond`)
    ELSE NOTHING
